    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b0dbdf03_241c1c87",
        "filename": "board/cr50/u2f.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 126,
      "author": {
        "id": 1324172
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-07-13T22:24:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "we can always read out drbg_entropy_size as actual size of data. For old keys it is 32 bytes (non-FIPS mode), in FIPS mode we generate it as 64 byte, the rest of key gen is not changed. So, this value is current size of the seed and not an indicator of mode, though have direct relation to FIPS mode. \nI was tempted to just check for 0, but then made it more complex to accommodate potentially invalid values which should never happen, unless under attack, and I want to be sure it can\u0027t be used to compromise security, say be setting it to 1-byte value with some carefully crafted nvmem attack using brownout behavior or something like that. It adds few bytes to code.",
      "parentUuid": "2ca805ce_0448b424",
